
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Assignment 11 - Graphics and Multimedia</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Graphics and Multimedia</h1>
        <p>WEB110 - Assignment 11</p>
    </header>

    <main>

        <section>
            <h2>Raster Graphics</h2>
            <p>This is my raster image.</p>

            <img src="sun-picture.png"
                 alt="Sunny landscape with a yellow sun, white clouds, blue sky, and green hills">
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Vector Graphics</h2>
            <p>This is my vector image.</p>

            <img src="vector-image.svg" alt="My vector graphic">
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Audio</h2>

            <audio controls>
                <source src="audio.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
                <source src="audio.oga" type="audio/ogg">
                Your browser does not support audio.
            </audio>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Video</h2>

            <video controls width="500">
                <source src="video.webm" type="video/webm">
                <source src="video.ogv" type="video/ogg">
                <source src="video.mp4" type="video/mp4">
                Your browser does not support video.
            </video>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>YouTube Video</h2>

            <iframe
                width="560"
                height="315"
                src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/tgbNymZ7vqY"
                title="YouTube video"
                allowfullscreen>
            </iframe>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>What I Learned</h2>

            <p>
                In this assignment, I learned about raster graphics,
                vector graphics, and multimedia. Raster graphics are
                made of pixels, while vector graphics use shapes and
                lines. I also learned how to add images, audio, and
                videos to a webpage using HTML. These skills can help
                me create more interesting websites and work with
                different types of graphics.
            </p>
        </section>

    </main>

</body>
</html>
